# Shared registries every parallel branch appends to (25 merge conflicts in the
# 14-15 Nov wave, 19 of them in these two files).
#
# CHANGELOG.md: a branch no longer adds bullets here, it adds a fragment,
# changelog.d/<alias>.md (changelog.d/README.md); the release preparation folds
# them in. The union merge stays for what is still edited by hand: the loose
# bullets of [Unreleased] from before fragments, and the fold itself. GitHub
# ignores merge drivers, which is why the fragments exist.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
# The per-package changelogs take fragments too (changelog.d/<package>/).
# public-source.json: path sets merged as data by a three-way driver. It needs
# the local git config once per clone (worktrees share it):
#   python3 tools/packaging/merge_public_source.py --install
# Without it git falls back to the line merge.
tools/packaging/public-source.json merge=public-source
# .sandloom/inspection.json (this project's and every example's): `sandloom
# generate` writes one record per line, so two branches that each add a module
# add different lines and git merges them; where both land in one gap the
# lines of both are kept (`union`), and the file reads the same in any order.
# Like the changelog above, GitHub's merge button ignores it: merge main locally.
# `text eol=lf`: a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf) keeps the lines LF.
**/.sandloom/inspection.json merge=union text eol=lf
